// Friends in Kishkindha — kishkindha kanda
// Source: Valmiki, Kishkindha Kanda, sargas 1-8 (verify)
// Migrated from the old script format. Not yet staged for the Ramlila stage.

>> scene kishkindha style=bharni-earth
>> music vanara
>> cast rama:exile at 0.26
>> cast lakshmana:exile at 0.16
Mount Rishyamukha. From the top, the exiled monkey king Sugriva sees two men with bows, and is sure his brother Vali has sent them.
>> enter hanuman from right to 0.62 in 1.4
He sends his minister down to find out. Hanuman comes dressed as a wandering beggar.
HANUMAN: You have the arms of kings and the dress of hermits, and you look at this forest as if you had lost something in it. Who are you? I am asked to ask.
RAMA: Lakshmana, answer him kindly. No one speaks like that who has not learned the three Vedas. Not a word out of place, and not one too many.
LAKSHMANA: We are the sons of Dasharatha. My brother's wife has been stolen. We were told that Sugriva could help us, and that we could help him.
>> pose hanuman namaste
HANUMAN: Then I am Hanuman, son of the Wind, and you have just made my king very happy. Climb on my shoulders.
>> scene kishkindha clear
>> prop fire altar at 0.5 scale=0.7
>> enter rama:exile from left to 0.36 in 0.1
>> enter sugriva from right to 0.64 in 0.1
>> enter hanuman from right to 0.84 in 0.1
>> enter lakshmana:exile from left to 0.2 in 0.1
Hanuman lights a fire. Rama and Sugriva walk around it, and are friends.
SUGRIVA: Your grief is mine now, and mine is yours. And I think I have something that belongs to you. It fell out of the sky.
>> prop bundle bundle at 0.5 y=-70 front=true raw=true
>> play tapSpots \{"hint":"friends.9","spots":\[\{"at":0.44,"y":130,"icon":"ornament","label":"friends.10","text":"friends.11"\},\{"at":0.5,"y":150,"icon":"ornament","label":"friends.12","text":"friends.13"\},\{"at":0.56,"y":130,"icon":"ornament","label":"friends.14","text":"friends.15"\}\]\}
LAKSHMANA: I do not know the earrings, or the bracelets. I know the anklets. I saw them every morning, when I bowed at her feet.
>> pose rama grieve
>> wait 1
SUGRIVA: I had a wife too, and a kingdom. My brother Vali took both, and would have had my life. No one can stand against Vali.
>> pose rama stand
RAMA: Someone can.
>> wash
-> END
